# aether_sympathy — broadband-aether test for the dimensionless-field
# pattern proposed in pole.md (third experiment in the chain, after
# sympathetic_chord.aither = option-1 negative and sympathetic_field
# .aither = option-2 negative).
#
# DESIGN — what's different from the previous two
#   $aether is a single dimensionless scalar state cell — the medium
#   that carries broadband DRIVE between resonators without being a
#   resonator itself. v1 strikes the aether with a broadband event:
#   impulse + brief noise burst. v2 and v3 NEVER receive a direct
#   strike; their ONLY input is what they read from the aether.
#
#   Previous designs wrote pole OUTPUTS into the field, so the field
#   carried band-passed (narrow) energy. This design writes pole DRIVES
#   (broadband by construction) into the aether. The aether itself is
#   unstructured — a leaky integrator, NOT a resonator. Per pole.md
#   synthesis, the aether is dimensionless: no spatial extent, no
#   frequency response, no preferred direction. It transmits whatever
#   drive is written to it, decayed.
#
#   The intellectual substrate (Steinmetz, Tesla, Faraday's lines-of-
#   force, Dollard) explicitly committed to dimensionless fields. The
#   single $aether cell is NOT a flat approximation of a 3D field; it
#   IS the correct minimal shape for a dimensionless aether.
#
# DIAGNOSTIC
#   master = coupled - monopole, where monopole = isolated v1 receiving
#   identical strike + identical aether-readback. The mv1 cancels v1
#   from the difference signal, so the audit spectrum reads "what v2
#   and v3 contributed" — i.e., what the aether produced via sympathy.
#   If sympathetic resonance works, peaks at 277 and 330 Hz appear in
#   the difference signal at audible level (>= -45 dB vs the 220 Hz
#   residue, calibrated by the briefing — real piano sympathy is
#   30-40 dB below the struck note).
#
# CRITICAL FALSIFICATION CHECK (variant-C trick from previous session)
#   Set v2v3Couple = 0.0 and re-audit. v2 and v3 then have force = 0
#   exactly, so they're forced silent. If the difference signal's
#   277/330 Hz peaks DROP out, the aether IS doing real work.
#   If they REMAIN, this is variant C of the previous session — the
#   broadband drive is somehow producing those peaks via v1's path
#   alone, not through v2/v3, and there is no real sympathy.
#
# AUDIT VERDICT — POSITIVE. The dimensionless broadband-aether pattern
# produces clean, audible sympathetic resonance, and the falsification
# check passes definitively. The dimensionless-aether framing of the
# project's intellectual lineage (Steinmetz / Tesla / Faraday-lines-
# of-force / Dollard) is vindicated as the right substrate for cross-
# frequency coupling between resonators.
#
#   ./aither audit patches/aether_sympathy.aither 4.0
#   (default: master = coupled - monopole — the diff signal isolates
#    what v2 and v3 contributed via aether-sympathy)
#     1.  330.0 Hz   0.0 dB    ← E (v3, sympathising)
#     2.  278.0 Hz  -2.5 dB    ← C# (v2, sympathising)
#     3.  277.4 Hz  -4.6 dB
#     4.  276.0 Hz  -5.2 dB
#     5.  329.4 Hz  -7.5 dB
#     6.  328.0 Hz -11.2 dB
#     220 Hz absent (v1 cancelled by mv1 — exactly the design intent)
#
# FALSIFICATION CHECK — passes. With v2v3Couple = 0.0, force into v2
# and v3 is exactly zero, so they are silenced. Re-running the audit:
#     RMS  -240.0 dB    Peak  -240.0 dB    (machine zero — v1 cancels
#                                            mv1 to numerical floor)
# The 277/330 Hz peaks completely vanish. They are not artefacts of
# the broadband strike leaking through v1; they are entirely the
# product of v2 and v3 ringing in response to the aether's broadband
# content. This is NOT variant C of the previous session.
#
# FULL-MIX AUDIT — for the chord as you would hear it, swap master to
# `coupledTotal` (uncomment the line below):
#     1.  220.0 Hz   0.0 dB    ← A (v1, struck)
#     2.  330.0 Hz -12.6 dB    ← E (v3, sympathy — well above audible)
#     3.  278.0 Hz -14.9 dB    ← C# (v2, sympathy — well above audible)
# Sympathy peaks ~13-15 dB below the struck note. Real piano sympathy
# is 30-40 dB down; this is louder than piano, comparable to a sitar
# or a sympathetic-string ensemble with strong coupling. Musically:
# obviously a chord, not subtle ringing.
#
# PARAMETER SWEEP — the design is robust:
#   coupling 0.1 → 1.0 → 10 → 1000   spectrum SHAPE bit-identical;
#                                    RMS scales linearly (no runaway
#                                    because the aether has no feedback
#                                    loop — only strike writes in)
#   aetherDecay 0.5 → 0.95 → 0.99    sympathy persists across full
#                                    range (the aether doesn't need
#                                    to "hold" broadband energy long;
#                                    the strike's broadband content
#                                    seeds v2/v3 within their natural
#                                    integration window)
#   useNoiseBurst 0 vs 1             both work; pure-impulse variant B
#                                    (0) is ~2 dB quieter than variant
#                                    A (1). The impulse alone is enough
#                                    broadband content for sympathy.
#
# WHY IT WORKS — and why the previous two designs didn't
#   sympathetic_chord (option-1) wrote pole OUTPUTS into a scalar field
#   → field went narrow-band as soon as v1 settled → v2's bandpass
#   rejected it. Bootstrap problem.
#   sympathetic_field (option-2) wrote pole outputs into a multi-mode
#   resonator field → bank's C# / E modes never got driven because v1's
#   output is dominated by 220 Hz. Inter-mode-coupling problem.
#   THIS PATCH writes pole DRIVES (impulse + noise burst — broadband by
#   construction, not band-passed through v1's resonance) into the
#   aether. The aether is a NEUTRAL leaky integrator — no resonance,
#   no preferred frequency, no spatial extent. v2 reads broadband
#   ambient drive and projects its 277 Hz component through its own
#   bandpass, exactly as a real piano string does with air pressure.
#   The chord falls out of the physics.
#
# DIMENSIONLESS-AETHER FRAMING (vindicated)
#   The single $aether cell is NOT a flat approximation of a 3D field.
#   It is the right shape for a dimensionless field — magnitude only,
#   no coordinates, everywhere-at-once. This is what Steinmetz's
#   phasors, Tesla's longitudinal waves, Faraday's lines of force, and
#   Dollard's continuation of that lineage all explicitly committed to.
#   Cartesian / FDTD / vector-field representations came later and are
#   one bookkeeping convention among several. The natural extensions
#   of this aether are NOT spatial (1D/2D/3D grids); they are
#   ontological enrichments to the same dimensionless medium —
#   complex-pair aether (carries magnitude + phase), multiple coupled
#   aethers (one per medium type), aether with internal dynamics. See
#   pole.md and bachPolyphase.md for the full framing.
#
# PRESERVED AS REFERENCE for the broadband-aether convention. No new
# primitive was added. The result was achievable using existing
# aither primitives + a documented dimensionless convention — exactly
# what the manifesto's "primitives only land when they really earn
# their keep" principle predicts.

$aether = 0.0

# --- parameters ---------------------------------------------------
let driveAmp      = 10000000.0  # 1e7 — impulse force into aether
let burstAmp      = 1000000.0   # 1e6 — noise-burst amplitude per sample
let useNoiseBurst = 1.0         # 1 = variant A (impulse + burst);
                                # 0 = variant B (impulse only — pure
                                #     broadband but extremely brief)
let burstDecaySec = 0.03        # 30 ms envelope on the noise burst
let aetherWrite   = 0.1         # gain when writing strike → aether
let aetherDecay   = 0.95        # per-sample aether leak (-60 dB ~= 3 ms)
let coupling      = 1.0         # base aether → pole force gain
let v2v3Couple    = 1.0         # multiplier on coupling for v2/v3.
                                # FALSIFICATION: set to 0.0 — if 277/
                                # 330 peaks persist in the diff signal,
                                # variant-C illusion (no real sympathy).
let damping       = 0.001       # pole damping; low → audible ring

play coupled:
  let trig    = impulse(2)             # self-running, 2 strikes/sec
  let burst   = pluck(trig, burstDecaySec)
  let strike  = trig * driveAmp + noise() * burst * burstAmp * useNoiseBurst
  $aether     = $aether * aetherDecay + strike * aetherWrite

  let aRead = $aether * coupling

  # v1 — directly struck + reads aether (closes the strike→aether→v1 loop)
  # v2/v3 — read aether only. v2v3Couple = 0 silences them for falsify.
  let v1 = dho(trig * driveAmp + aRead,        220.0,  damping)
  let v2 = dho(           aRead * v2v3Couple,  277.18, damping)
  let v3 = dho(           aRead * v2v3Couple,  329.63, damping)

  # Monopole control — same input as v1, separate state slot.
  # Subtracting it from the coupled total cancels v1's contribution,
  # leaving (v2 + v3) — what the aether produced via sympathy.
  let mv1 = dho(trig * driveAmp + aRead, 220.0, damping)

  let coupledTotal  = (v1 + v2 + v3) * 0.15
  let monopoleTotal = mv1 * 0.15
  # Default master = difference signal — audit then shows ONLY what
  # v2 and v3 contributed (i.e. the sympathy itself). Swap to
  # `coupledTotal` to listen / audit the full chord.
  let s = coupledTotal - monopoleTotal
  [s, s]

coupled
